	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE D1:\nTwo ADS8689, one per read-back signal, on the shared isolated SPI with their own chip selects (ISO_CS_ADC on J3 pin 11, ISO_CS_ADC2 on J3 pin 15, both on the default-HIGH isolator U44). I and V are sampled in the same instant, there is no analog switch in the path and the firmware is the same driver twice (decision 2026-11-08, replaces the single ADC + CD74HC4052 mux). VMID_REF is a DC constant (LM4040 0.1 % x 1 % divider): measure it once on TP29 [9] and subtract in software; it is not digitised."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 203.2 0)
		(size 62 22)
		(margins 1 1 1 1)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "91f67073-3690-4f17-8fd0-6ee951ca80f7")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE D2:\nRange 0-5.12 V (1.25 x VREF): VMID + 0.2 V/mA uses 13-52 % of full scale, 0.39 uA/LSB, noise-free ~13 bits [DS SNR 92 dB]; V_elec 7.9 mV/LSB. The input is a 1 MOhm resistive divider rated +/-20 V [DS], so a saturated OPA4192 on [9] needs no clamp. Rev 2 option: use the bipolar +/-2.56 V range and drop the VMID adder on [9]."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 106.68 203.2 0)
		(size 62 17)
		(margins 1 1 1 1)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b3d8bb41-9a46-4968-80b1-977c13bb0f8f")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE D3:\nSupplies drawn at the pins in layout order: +5V -> 10 uF -> 1 uF -> AVDD; +3V3 -> 1 uF -> DVDD [DS 8.3.1]. AVDD must be 4.75-5.25 V; DVDD could be 5 V as well, but 3.3 V keeps the SPI at Red Pitaya levels for the J5 bypass and matches the isolator side 2 and the DAC DVCC. Reference: internal 4.096 V, 10 uF on REFIO, 1 uF nearest REFCAP then 10 uF, returned to REFGND [DS]. RST shared, pulled up by R85; GPO / RVS not used (NC). SDO-0 is tri-state while CS is high, so both ADCs and the DAC share ISO_MISO [DS]."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 106.68 222.25 0)
		(size 62 22)
		(margins 1 1 1 1)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8c78e8ce-1628-4368-92a5-82460c1c99af")
	)
	(text_box "LAYOUT NOTE L1:\nPer ADC: 1 uF then 10 uF at REFCAP (pin 6), 10 uF at REFIO (pin 4), returns to REFGND (pin 5) and the plane under the part; 1 uF at AVDD and DVDD, via at the pad; 10 nF across pins 7-8. Keep I_RETURN_ADC / V_ELEC_ADC from [9] away from the SPI traces; route the bus on the digital side of both parts. AGND, DGND, REFGND: one plane."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 172.72 203.2 0)
		(size 62 17)
		(margins 1 1 1 1)
		(stroke
